Structural Check
- [S1] STC9 failed: Each branch node must have exactly one incoming and at least two outgoing edges. | Node `b1` has in=1 and out=1. | Node `b2` has in=1 and out=1. | DSL: branch(b1,XOR); branch(b2,XOR)
- [S2] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v1` has an invalid range `['no']`. | Variable `v2` has an invalid range `['no']`.
- [S3] STC15 failed: Every variable used in a guard must be formally defined. | Guard `v1 = 'no'` on `b1 -> n4` uses undefined variable `v1`. | Guard `v2 = 'no'` on `b2 -> n5` uses undefined variable `v2`. | DSL: guard(b1,n4,"v1 = 'no'"); guard(b2,n5,"v2 = 'no'")

Logical Sanity Check
- [L1] LSC1 failed: Every guard must be satisfiable under the declared ranges of its referenced variables. | Guard `v1 = 'no'` on `b1 -> n4` cannot be evaluated: `v1` has no declared range. | Guard `v2 = 'no'` on `b2 -> n5` cannot be evaluated: `v2` has no declared range. | DSL: guard(b1,n4,"v1 = 'no'"); guard(b2,n5,"v2 = 'no'")
- [L2] LSC3 failed: Guards outgoing from XOR/OR branches must cover the whole evaluated state space. | Branch `b1` cannot be evaluated: `v1` has no declared range. | Branch `b2` cannot be evaluated: `v2` has no declared range.
